WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:02.320
Steven Lawrence was murdered

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.900
because he was Black.

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.890
Few crimes in recent times have had

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:09.000
such a profound or long lasting impact.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.870
Injustice, watershed, landmark

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:14.770
are all used to describe
the Lawrence Case.

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:18.590
The thing that makes Lawrence
particularly important

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:21.370
and why I think the Stephen
Lawrence case is the case

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:25.700
that is apparently changed
the nation is because

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.030
it hinges on something else.

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:31.940
So the murder itself was just jaw dropping

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.861
and nobody could grasp that.

00:00:34.861 --> 00:00:39.861
But what followed was just
beyond anybody's imagination.

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:49.550
I remember the Stephen
Lawrence case very well.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:52.050
It was the day before
my daughter's birthday.

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:54.490
So it was the 22nd of April, 1993,

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:57.310
and I remember it extremely well.

00:00:57.310 --> 00:00:59.820
It's hard to describe it in any other way

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:03.360
as just almost sport.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.130
I suspect, for an American audience,

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:08.350
you would be able to
really relate to this,

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:10.500
and perhaps this is why it was so shocking

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:14.060
because although it wasn't,
in any sense, a kind of,

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:17.310
you know, down south Mississippi lynching,

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.300
it wasn't far off.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.130
This is the bus stop
where Stephen Lawrence

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:24.580
was brutally stabbed to death
in a savage racial attack.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:26.650
Today, the bus stops being changed,

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:28.230
there are even new benches,

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:30.550
but it does nothing to diminish the fact

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:33.590
that this point represents the very worst

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:35.530
in British race relations.

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:38.210
You had two boys, Stephen and his friend,

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:41.900
who were at a bus stop in
Southeast London one evening.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:46.900
And they were part of a
absolutely unprovoked attack

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:51.390
where one of the boys managed to escape.

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:52.830
Stephen, sadly, didn't.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:57.830
And five young white men murdered him.

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:01.890
And as we discovered as the story unfolds

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:05.620
and the press and the media are
able to get behind the story

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:08.530
of Stephen's murderers,

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:11.340
these people had practiced
these kinds of assaults

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.810
and killings in their bedrooms.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.570
And also, it was just the
most extraordinary thing.

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:17.490
And it was the premeditated nature of it

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:20.613
that I think people found
so very, very difficult.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:24.690
In the days following Stephen's murder,

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:27.230
the police received several tip-offs

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:31.150
and all sources pointed
to the same five suspects,

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:34.520
brothers, Neil and Jamie
Acourt, Gary Dobson,

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:37.610
Luke Knight, and David Norris.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:39.930
Their gang were named 26 times

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.760
as Stephen Lawrence's killers

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.730
in the hours following his murder.

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:46.780
Lawrence handed in her
own list of suspects

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:49.300
only to see the officer first fold it up

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:51.903
and then strew it into
a ball in front of her.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:54.580
The Met's failure to respond

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:57.950
to initial reports would
prove to be the first

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:01.750
in a string of injustices
against the Lawrence family

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:03.963
that spanned more than two decades.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:09.620
Couple of weeks later,
and still no arrests.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.910
The Lawrence family had a press conference

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:15.440
airing their frustration that
not enough was being done

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:16.823
to catch the killers.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.903
Two days later, they
met with Nelson Mandela.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:25.170
Nelson Mandela paused
on a visit to Britain

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:28.020
to publicly shake the Lawrence's hands.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:31.040
In private, they talked, he listened

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:32.933
when no one in authority would.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:37.750
We are very used to this type of thing

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:41.493
where life is regarded
as cheap in South Africa.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:45.590
And but, nevertheless,
it's a sense of disconcert

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:49.173
that it should happen in
a country like Britain.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:52.020
So we had these two huge problems.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:55.310
We had this issue of a
young man in a London street

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:56.600
who could be murdered,

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:59.170
but in addition to the murder,

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:02.140
we were confronted with
this extraordinary notion

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:07.140
of the ineptitude of the police inquiry

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:10.803
that was motivated by race.

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:15.043
It's a racist society
that it doesn't matter,

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:18.450
as for a Black person, that is,

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:19.940
it doesn't matter what standard of life

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:21.580
you try to achieve for yourself,

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:23.960
it makes no difference in cases like this.

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:25.390
You are treated as if you're a criminal

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:27.428
right from the start.

00:04:27.428 --> 00:04:30.420
In 1994, a year after the murder,

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:33.520
covert video filmed by the
police over several days

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:35.680
in one of the suspects apartments

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:37.710
showed the gang using knives

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.972
and making violent racist remarks.

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:45.490
With the investigation going nowhere,

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:48.860
and a growing sense that
the system had failed them,

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:52.123
Stephen's parents took
matters into their own hands.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:56.160
In 1996, Doreen and
Neville Lawrence took out

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.283
a private prosecution
against three suspects.

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:02.750
This was the first private prosecution

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:05.883
for murder in the UK
for more than a century.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:10.683
But the Lawrence's would once
again leave without justice.

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:13.390
The judge directed the jury

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:15.640
to return not guilty verdicts.

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:18.640
Identification evidence
was ruled inadmissible,

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:20.610
and there was not enough other evidence

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:22.203
to justify the prosecution.

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:25.580
The three suspects were acquitted

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:28.730
and the entering of not
guilty verdicts meant

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:30.683
they could not be tried again.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:34.200
I think one of the things that
makes the racism arguments

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:37.970
such an interesting one is
that there is the difference,

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:41.510
I think, between individual
racism and institutional racism.

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:45.910
So, and I think that most
people would be askance

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:49.100
at the idea of being
accused of being racist,

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:52.970
but because we live so
comfortably in a racist system,

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:56.080
it's difficult to
reconcile those two points

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:58.280
because self-evidently
the system is racist.

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:02.210
In 1997, the Lawrence family registered

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:06.080
a formal complaint with the
Police Complaints Authority

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:08.633
about the Met's handling
of the investigation.

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:13.440
Soon after, "The Daily
Mail", a national newspaper,

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:17.640
ran a front page accusing
the men of killing Lawrence

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.923
and challenging them to sue for libel.

00:06:22.437 --> 00:06:24.250
I think "The Daily Mail's" involvement

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:26.180
was really very surprising.

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:27.013
If you think about "The Daily Mail",

00:06:27.013 --> 00:06:28.920
"The Daily Mail's" sort of Fox News

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:31.680
of the UK broadcasting environment,

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:34.429
and this was very much a CNN story,

00:06:34.429 --> 00:06:36.863
if I can put it that way for you.

00:06:36.863 --> 00:06:39.940
And the fact that it
was actually Fox News,

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:42.820
in the form of "The Daily
Mail" that went to bat on this,

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:46.990
and actually published the
extraordinary headline "Murders,"

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:51.053
with a picture of these young
men was a massive stunt.

00:06:54.064 --> 00:06:55.670
With growing interest around the case,

00:06:55.670 --> 00:06:58.330
from both the media and the public,

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:01.540
pressure was on the newly
elected Labor administration

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:02.633
to take action.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:08.980
By the summer of 1997, the
new Home Secretary Jack Straw

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:10.740
met with the Lawrences.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:14.450
And soon after the Home Office
announced a judicial inquiry

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:17.220
into the police's handling of the case.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:19.340
This inquiry will have full powers

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:21.140
to compel the attendance of witnesses,

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:22.770
to give evidence under oath,

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:24.390
and if they fail to do so,

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:27.103
to punish them as if it
were a contempt of court.

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:31.150
The inquiry, led by
retired High Court Judge

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:32.900
Sir William MacPherson,

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:37.900
sat for 59 days to hear
evidence from 88 witnesses

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:42.433
and produced more than
100,000 pages of documents.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:46.190
At the heart of this
inquiry is the allegation

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:48.000
from the Lawrence's and their lawyers

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.750
that racism permeated
the police investigation

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:53.500
into Stephen's death and
permeates the society

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:54.900
in which happened.

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:57.800
So it's become a touchstone
for the Black community,

00:07:57.800 --> 00:07:59.900
and the outcome could
point to the direction

00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:02.970
to the future of race
relations in Britain.

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:04.920
The gang came to give evidence

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.380
at the public hearing,

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:10.790
having been told they will
face prosecution otherwise.

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:13.630
A huge crowd gathered outside the hearing,

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:16.516
hoping to get a chance to
see them take the stands.

00:08:16.516 --> 00:08:17.349
What do we want?

00:08:17.349 --> 00:08:18.182
Justice!

00:08:18.182 --> 00:08:19.015
Who for?

00:08:19.015 --> 00:08:19.848
Stephen Lawrence.

00:08:19.848 --> 00:08:20.681
At the inquest,

00:08:20.681 --> 00:08:23.940
the five suspects refused
to answer questions.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:27.360
The inquest jury ruled Stephen
had been unlawfully killed

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:30.293
in a completely unprovoked racist attack.

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:34.530
Tensions between the police, the public,

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:38.920
and the suspects reached
boiling point outside the court.

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:41.690
The inquiry was adjourned for three hours

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:44.873
after police fired CS gas on protesters.

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:51.840
The men spat and hit out at the crowd

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:54.853
while police escorted them
back to their vehicles.

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:03.120
In 1999, two years
after the inquiry began,

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:06.120
MacPherson made 70 recommendations

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:09.748
and delivered a damning final verdict.

00:09:09.748 --> 00:09:14.748
He conclude it in his
really landmark report

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:18.440
that the Metropolitan Police Service

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:20.633
was indeed institutionally racist.

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:26.800
There 70 kind of overarching
recommendations were presented

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:28.670
to the Metropolitan Police Force,

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:31.670
and the Metropolitan
Police Force, to be honest,

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:34.583
has been having a very,

00:09:36.676 --> 00:09:39.330
a very complicated time engaging with it.

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:40.610
The chairman of the inquiry,

00:09:40.610 --> 00:09:43.120
Sir William MacPherson
repeatedly challenged Sir Paul

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:46.120
about widespread instinctive
racism within the force,

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.883
but Sir Paul continually
rebutted that suggestion.

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:52.070
I find it difficult after five years

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:54.400
for the commissioner to still be saying

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:57.220
that he felt that there was no racism

00:09:57.220 --> 00:09:59.493
or corruption involved in Stephen's case.

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:04.080
So if that wasn't racism
and it wasn't corruption,

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.210
I still haven't been given the answer

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:09.593
as to why Stephen's killers
are still walking free.

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:14.860
The inquiry prompted some serious changes

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:16.360
within the police force

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:20.800
and led to the Race Relations
Amendment Act in 2000

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:23.650
that strive to eliminate discrimination

00:10:23.650 --> 00:10:25.583
and promote racial equality.

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:30.490
But the problem of racism is

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:37.280
it's so deeply woven into
the fabric of our society

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:41.903
that it is by no means a
simple thing to resolve.

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:45.420
The inquiry may have shone light

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:49.330
on institutional racism, but
it didn't bring the result

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:52.450
the Lawrence family so desperately wanted,

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:55.123
the conviction of their son's murderers.

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:57.410
In the 11 years since,

00:10:57.410 --> 00:10:59.780
there have been three
murder investigations,

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:02.450
two police reviews, and a public inquiry,

00:11:02.450 --> 00:11:05.160
yet his killers still remain free.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:07.080
Now the Crown Prosecution Service says

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:09.893
it's unlikely the case
will ever be solved.

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:14.470
But then in 2005, double jeopardy,

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:17.590
the rule preventing
suspects being tried twice

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:20.640
for the same crime, was scrapped.

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:22.800
Something MacPherson had recommended

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:25.620
in his report six years earlier.

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:27.560
But with no new evidence,

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:30.163
this offered the Lawrence
family little hope.

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:35.690
At every turn, the Lawrence
Case makes history.

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:39.840
They literally challenged
every step of the way

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:41.740
and whatever obstacle was in the place,

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:45.770
statute, law and so and so,
they just overturned it.

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:48.020
A tiny spot of blood found on the collar

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:51.390
of Dobson's jacket has a
one in a billion chance

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:53.540
of not belonging to Stephen.

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:55.990
Other fibers from the dead
teenagers clothing were

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:58.673
allegedly found on a
multicolored cardigan.

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:03.030
Using the latest forensic technology,

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:06.000
new evidence was found
during a cold case review

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.110
of Lawrence's murder that tied

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:11.023
two the previously acquitted
suspects to the case.

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:16.270
In 2011, the trial of Gary
Dobson and David Norris

00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:20.253
for Lawrence's murder begins
in light of the new evidence.

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:25.200
It took a long time
for justice to ride out

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:26.640
in the Lawrence Case.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:29.250
Doreen watched the many
suspects in her son's murder

00:12:29.250 --> 00:12:32.090
walk free from courts and inquiries.

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:35.800
19 years later, only two of
them have been convicted,

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:39.583
a failure, she says, of
politicians, as well as the police.

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:46.110
It's 19 years later, 19
years, let me say that again,

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:49.800
before Dobson and Norris were imprisoned.

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:52.087
So there are two things about
that that are extraordinary.

00:12:52.087 --> 00:12:54.240
One is it took 19 years for them

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:59.240
to be brought to court again
and charged and found guilty.

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:02.163
Ans two is that 19 years later,

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:05.450
Baroness Lawrence was still as resilient

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:09.873
and as committed to it as
she was 19 years previously.

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:14.500
We pay tribute to Mr. and Mrs. Lawrence's

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:16.053
courage and dignity.

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:21.260
They have contributed to
major changes within policing,

00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:25.203
the law, and indeed
within society as a whole.

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:28.650
Doreen Lawrence continued to campaign

00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:30.590
for justice for her son,

00:13:30.590 --> 00:13:33.713
as well as for other
victims of racist crime.

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:39.740
In 2013, Doreen was awarded
the title of Baroness

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:41.948
for her relentless work
within the community.

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:50.100
She has been, you know,
really, really, really embedded

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:53.160
in the psyche of this
nation because of the work

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:55.380
that she's done and the
sacrifice she's paid.

00:13:55.380 --> 00:13:58.930
It's hard to explain it in
terms of what it looks like,

00:13:58.930 --> 00:14:00.550
but it was, it was...

00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:05.550
Yeah, in a way it was our
probably the most important

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:07.740
criminal justice struggle,

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:10.330
in terms of the Black
story in this country

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:12.173
in the last, however many years.

00:14:13.640 --> 00:14:15.278
Black Lives Matter!

00:14:15.278 --> 00:14:16.380
Black Lives Matter!

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:18.920
Policing has long been a focal point

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:22.540
for concerns of racial
injustice in the UK.

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:25.630
And despite changes sparked
by the Lawrence case

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:28.370
and the landmark MacPherson inquiry,

00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:31.260
Black people and ethnic
minorities in Britain

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:34.110
are still disproportionately represented

00:14:34.110 --> 00:14:37.330
when it comes to police
checks, imprisonment,

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:38.843
and deaths in custody.

00:14:40.840 --> 00:14:43.550
We need to remember that
the UK is not innocent.

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:45.610
We are a physical representation

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:47.570
of our support for George Floyd.

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:49.650
